      <Docs>
        <summary>Returns the anchor height above floor uncertainty.</summary>
        <value>Value is between 0 and 24 inclusive</value>
        <remarks>
          <para>Returns the anchor height above floor uncertainty.</para>
          <para>An Anchor Height Above Floor Uncertainty value of 0 indicates an unknown anchor height above floor. Values 25 or higher are reserved.</para>
          <para>h − 2 ^ (11 - u) &lt;= a &lt;= h + 2 ^ (11 - u)</para>
          <para>where</para>
          <para>h is the value in units of 1/4096 m of the anchor Height Above Floor field</para>
          <para>u is the value of the Anchors Height Above Floor Uncertainty field</para>
          <para>If the Anchor Height Above Floor field indicates an unknown anchor height above floor, the Anchor Height Above Floor Uncertainty field is set to 0.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/ranging/DlTdoaMeasurement.ZElementExtension#getAnchorHeightAboveFloorUncertainty()" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.ranging.DlTdoaMeasurement.ZElementExtension.getAnchorHeightAboveFloorUncertainty</code>.</a></format></para>
